{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes and their probabilities, considering differences in outcomes as negligible and preferring the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. Here, the favorable outcome is defined as '0 Euros' (i.e., no loss), since both lotteries involve possible losses. Lottery A has a 99.8% chance of 0 Euros, while Lottery B has a 99.9% chance of 0 Euros. Thus, Lottery B has a slightly higher probability (by 0.1 percentage points) of the favorable outcome. The outcome differences (-3000 vs -6000) are present, but the reason treats such differences as negligible. Therefore, according to the decision reason, Lottery B should be preferred.",
